---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../utils/schema';

const hasEndpoint = Boolean(site.forms.contact || site.forms.review);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How this website handles information you choose to send to Amie Oren, in plain language."
  path="/privacy/"
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy' }])]}
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="Your privacy, in plain language." breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy' }]} />

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="container container--narrow prose">
      <p class="muted small">Last updated: October 1, 2026</p>

      <h2>What this site collects</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not use analytics, advertising pixels, tracking scripts, or a customer-management
        system, and it does not set cookies for tracking. The fonts and images it uses are served from the site
        itself.
      </p>
      <p>
        The only information the site receives is what you choose to send through its forms (Contact, Leave a
        Review, and Refer Someone): the details you enter, such as your name, email address, phone number, and
        message.
      </p>

      <h2>How form submissions work</h2>
      {
        hasEndpoint ? (
          <p>
            Form submissions are sent to a third-party form service, currently Formspree, which delivers them to
            me by email. That service processes your submission on its servers; its own privacy policy
            describes how it handles data. Submissions also arrive in my email inbox.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            Forms on this site prepare an email to me. Nothing is sent until you send the message from your
            own email application.
          </p>
        )
      }

      <h2>Find Your West Michigan Fit and saved searches</h2>
      <p>
        The Find Your West Michigan Fit guide runs entirely in your browser. Your answers are not collected,
        stored, or sent anywhere while you use it, and you don’t need to provide any contact information to see
        your results.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you choose “Send me homes that fit this,” your answers (as preference selections, such as water
        priority or lot preference) travel in the address of the saved-search page so the form can be filled in
        for you. They contain no personal information. When you submit the saved-search form, the details you
        enter, plus a short summary of your Find Your Fit selections and results, are sent to me through the
        form service described above. I use them to set up a saved search in my own listing system by hand. The
        site does not create listing alerts automatically.
      </p>

      <h2>How I use your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To reply to your message or inquiry.</li>
        <li>For saved-search requests: to set up a search for you and send matching homes.</li>
        <li>
          For reviews: to verify that a review is genuine. Reviews are never published automatically. I
          confirm them and your permission first, and your email address is never published.
        </li>
        <li>
          For referrals: to reach out to the person you introduced, in the way you suggested. Please share
          someone’s details only if they’re comfortable with it.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>I do not sell your information.</p>

      <h2>Emailing me directly</h2>
      <p>
        If you email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>, your message is handled
        by your email provider and mine, under their policies.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        This site may link to other websites. Their practices are their own, so please review their policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions or requests</h2>
      <p>
        To ask what information you have sent, or to ask for it to be deleted, email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}> {site.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this site later adds anything that affects privacy, such as analytics, this page will be updated
        before it goes live.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
